⟦⎊⟧ BotFather menu — logged, page by page
⋮⋮TPR.HUB⋮⋮

Every page BotFather shows, what it actually sets, the API method
that does it headless, where that config lives in a ZenBot pack,
and the doc that explains it. Logged ⧗-26.392 from the live menu.

── APIkey ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The token. NEVER written into a doc, a repo, or this hub.
  home    : TelePromptR/.station/vec3/lib/keys/<KEY_NAME>
  read by : run.py _load_token() · TPR_BOT_KEY names the file
  wall    : hands refuses */vec3/lib/keys/* — the keyring is
            walled for every seat, agents included
  tripwire: the digits BEFORE the colon are the bot id and are
            PUBLIC (getMe returns them). Bots/bots.kdl records
            the id, so a swapped token is detectable without
            anything reading the secret.
  revoke  : BotFather → /revoke — old token dies instantly
:: ∎

── Settings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
Edit Info      name · about · description · profile photo
  api    setMyName · setMyShortDescription · setMyDescription
  pack   copy.txt (the prose) · setup-bot.sh pushes it
  docs   https://core.telegram.org/bots/features#botfather
Commands       the slash menu, PER SCOPE
  api    setMyCommands (scope: default · all_private_chats ·
         all_group_chats · all_chat_administrators)
  pack   commands/{default,private,group,admin}.json
  docs   https://core.telegram.org/bots/features#commands
Mini Apps      the web app + the menu button that opens it
  api    setChatMenuButton {type: web_app, web_app: {url}}
  pack   miniapp/miniapp.json · served by run.py route /app
  law    Telegram loads a Mini App IN THE USER'S CLIENT, so the
         URL must be PUBLIC. A tailnet host works for Lucius and
         for nobody else.
  docs   https://core.telegram.org/bots/webapps
Bot Settings   privacy · groups · inline · payments toggles
  api    mostly BotFather-only; getMe REPORTS the result
         (can_join_groups · can_read_all_group_messages)
  pack   privacy/privacy.json · groups/groups.json ·
         inline/inline.json · modes/modes.json
  seen   @ender_zenbot has privacy OFF — reads-all=true
  docs   https://core.telegram.org/bots/features#privacy-mode
Login Widget   web auth by Telegram identity
  api    no method — a JS widget + server-side hash check
  pack   TPR.HUB/TPR.HUB (domain zensen.live, flow written)
  docs   https://core.telegram.org/bots/telegram-login
Serverless     Telegram-hosted bot logic (new)
  note   NOT how TPR runs. TPR is a station on en0 metal behind
         a webhook. Logged so the page is not a mystery.
  docs   https://core.telegram.org/bots/serverless
Games          HTML5 games served through the bot
  api    sendGame · setGameScore
  note   unused. No pack folder until there is a game.
  docs   https://core.telegram.org/bots/games
:: ∎

── Monetization ───────────────────────────────────────────────
Payments        real money · a provider token per currency
  api    sendInvoice · answerPreCheckoutQuery
  note   a live money path. Nothing automated touches it.
  docs   https://core.telegram.org/bots/payments
Telegram Stars  in-app currency · digital goods · subscriptions
  api    sendInvoice with currency XTR · no provider needed
  why    the shortest paid door for a relay: charge Stars per
         seat instead of eating the compute
  docs   https://core.telegram.org/bots/payments-stars
:: ∎

── Actions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Transfer Ownership   moves the bot to another Telegram account
  note   the point of @tpr_zenbot is that groups own their room,
         not that ownership moves. Nothing here needs this.
Delete Bot           irreversible · frees the username
  note   the username is the asset. Deleting @<name>_zenbot
  		 hands it back to the pool.
:: ∎

── Order to walk it, for a new bot ────────────────────────────
1 /newbot → name → @<name>_zenbot  (BotFather decides free)
2 token → the vault path above, nothing else
3 bin/new-zenbot <name> → scaffolds the pack + registers it
4 ZenBots/<Name>/setup-bot.sh → pushes Edit Info + Commands
5 BotFather by hand: Groups · Privacy · Inline · Mini App URL
6 getMe → confirm what actually took (setup-bot.sh prints it)
:: ∎
